VALUES ('broad-default-acceleration-clause', 'Broad Default Acceleration Clause', 'termination', 'high', 'Allows the lender to declare the entire loan balance due immediately for minor, non-financial reasons, such as the lender ''feeling insecure'' or a minor technical breach of a reporting requirement.', 'Gives the lender too much power to force a borrower into default even if they are making all payments on time. It can be used as leverage to force unfavorable renegotiations.', 'They can demand you pay back the whole loan today just because they ''feel'' like you might not pay later, even if you''ve never missed a payment.', 'Acceleration should only be permitted for material breaches (e.g., non-payment) after a 15-day grace period and written notice.', 'We''d like to limit the acceleration clause to material defaults like non-payment, and ensure we have at least 15 days to fix any issues before the full balance is called.', 'Lender may only accelerate the unpaid balance of the Loan in the event of a material default (defined as non-payment of principal or interest) that remains uncured for fifteen (15) days after written notice is provided to the Borrower.', '[-0.000116519,-0.02919933,0.0322531,0.03439628,-0.029966926,0.014873643,0.00905506,-0.034948923,-0.021167792,-0.019689457,0.027121209,0.046765838,0.037712306,0.037823644,0.04022807,-0.03177724,-0.030103737,0.038673688,-0.016115416,-0.033588693,-0.008163245,-0.020152237,0.0008282839,-0.026445674,-0.04421841,-0.043530036,-0.033623595,-0.011774675,-0.047594223,-0.06545902,-0.017386349,0.0059898333,-0.025373895,-0.059719443,0.0036050663,0.002674412,-0.028281739,0.023938477,0.023171077,-0.03051908,-0.02896758,0.036990713,-0.032762717,0.016131835,-0.020922996,-0.016536929,0.039198563,-0.024639199,-0.01434534,0.065261476,0.043025788,0.04353513,-0.05023115,0.0027472451,0.039300304,-0.021803679,-0.03669058,-0.025105448,-0.013314181,0.059172012,0.013389015,-0.009989798,0.020020302,0.03193116,0.07671425,-0.03421912,-0.